From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 12:17:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Add a cross-resolve damage summary for partial-frame gating

Fold each resolve's per-node damage into a paint-only vs layout-class
summary (DamageSummary, capped at 64 nodes per list) exposed via
take_damage_summary. resolve takes it before non-incremental mode marks
everything damaged, so it reflects real mutations and restyle diffs. An
embedder can use it to decide whether a frame is safe to rasterize as a
partial clip.

set_attribute stops eagerly OR-ing ALL_DAMAGE (an upstream TODO): the
restyle hint already drives a recascade whose
compute_style_difference produces the real damage, so a render-neutral
attribute write (data-*, aria-*) no longer looks like full layout
damage.
---
